{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20342",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.71,
      "end_seconds": 4.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Yeah, hi doctor, am I too early?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.33,
      "end_seconds": 10.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "Okay, no problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.42,
      "end_seconds": 21.07,
      "duration_seconds": 9.65,
      "text": "Okay, so I wanted to get nose bleeds looked at. My neighbour said I should get it looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.73,
      "end_seconds": 24.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.19,
      "end_seconds": 32.39,
      "duration_seconds": 6.2,
      "text": "Let me think, it's been going on for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.08,
      "end_seconds": 35.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "anything that improves it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.79,
      "end_seconds": 40.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "I get some relief from pinching my nose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.78,
      "end_seconds": 44.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Any other symptoms with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.72,
      "end_seconds": 67.69,
      "duration_seconds": 21.97,
      "text": "Indigestion after tablets goes along with it, you know, most of the time. And bruising easily, too. The Indigestion after tablets? That's been for two years. Hmm, with Indigestion after tablets, about a five out of ten. I've been feeling tired too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.93,
      "end_seconds": 72.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "How strong would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.85,
      "end_seconds": 73.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "Mostly moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.5,
      "end_seconds": 82.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.88,
      "text": "have you had nose bleeds before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.62,
      "end_seconds": 90.71,
      "duration_seconds": 7.09,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened last year, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.51,
      "end_seconds": 104.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "Any blood in the urine or palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.56,
      "end_seconds": 109.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "No, nothing to to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.23,
      "end_seconds": 116.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any black stools or breathlessness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.68,
      "end_seconds": 123.05,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "No, you know, I haven't had any of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.24,
      "end_seconds": 128.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "so, how are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.01,
      "end_seconds": 132.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "No, uh, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.51,
      "end_seconds": 147.08,
      "duration_seconds": 8.57,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.03,
      "end_seconds": 151.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "I've got diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.65,
      "end_seconds": 153.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "any other things?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.31,
      "end_seconds": 161.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.78,
      "text": "Yes, heart disease. I have high cholesterol, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.85,
      "end_seconds": 171.84,
      "duration_seconds": 9.99,
      "text": "Yes, carry on. Right, so heart disease is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.86,
      "end_seconds": 175.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "no, never"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.74,
      "end_seconds": 178.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.95,
      "end_seconds": 190.48,
      "duration_seconds": 9.53,
      "text": "I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.04,
      "end_seconds": 201.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.74,
      "end_seconds": 232.17,
      "duration_seconds": 29.43,
      "text": "hmm, I take sitagliptin, 100 milligrams, once a day i'm on metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day for my heart okay, um, so though honestly, some days I forget to take it. Simvastatin, 20 milligrams, at night i didn't want to make a fuss, you know i told my wife I'd come today"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.74,
      "end_seconds": 234.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.13,
      "end_seconds": 242.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.76,
      "end_seconds": 244.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.31,
      "end_seconds": 250.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.84,
      "end_seconds": 253.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.07,
      "end_seconds": 263.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.13,
      "end_seconds": 295.38,
      "duration_seconds": 11.25,
      "text": "Okay: SpO2 97 percent on room air, temperature 36.5, pressure 111 over 75, heart rate 79, weight 85 kilos, respiratory rate 18, height 177 centimetres."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.34,
      "end_seconds": 301.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.69,
      "end_seconds": 305.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "breathe out slowly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.55,
      "end_seconds": 316.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "There are a few small bruises on your forearms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.1,
      "end_seconds": 318.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.76,
      "end_seconds": 338.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal and your chest is clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.44,
      "end_seconds": 344.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "You can relax now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 351.66,
      "end_seconds": 362.27,
      "duration_seconds": 10.61,
      "text": "Okay, thinking it through, I can't pin this down yet. We're looking at stable coronary disease on antiplatelet treatment, with minor bleeding or angina."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 363.58,
      "end_seconds": 370.93,
      "duration_seconds": 7.35,
      "text": "Sorry, uh, what was I saying, do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 371.93,
      "end_seconds": 395.54,
      "duration_seconds": 23.61,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now stable coronary disease on antiplatelet treatment, with minor bleeding is my leading thought, not anything worse. I want a lipid profile done, that's for cardiovascular risk. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. I think blood tests makes sense here, for bruising and bleeding."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 396.8,
      "end_seconds": 407.87,
      "duration_seconds": 11.07,
      "text": "I'd like you to take pantoprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast, long term. You take it by mouth. That should help with stomach protection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 411.82,
      "end_seconds": 413.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "Okay, I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 415.36,
      "end_seconds": 426.26,
      "duration_seconds": 10.9,
      "text": "Take your blood-thinning tablets after food and do not stop them on your own. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 428.25,
      "end_seconds": 431.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 433.67,
      "end_seconds": 435.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}